{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py | tail -130; rg -n 'format|page_sha256|render_page|forg|passed' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py; tail -n 4 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md | cut -c1-850; sed -n '448,466p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"RELEASE-BUILD.md §6 mutants: each applied to a scratch copy (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE, no __pycache__) must fail\n     2\ttests/test_release.py; the unmutated control must pass.\"\"\"\n     3\timport shutil\n     4\timport subprocess\n     5\timport sys\n     6\timport tempfile\n     7\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     8\tfrom xml.etree import ElementTree\n     9\t\n    10\tREPO = Path('/Users/lchingen/hivemind')\n    11\tR, B = 'src/hivemind/release.py', 'scripts/release_build.py'\n    12\tMUTANTS = {\n    13\t    'condition emitted on number records': (R, \"                record['forecast'] = FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE\\n            else:\\n                record['answers'] = labels\\n                record['answer'] = _answer(\",\n    14\t                                            \"                record['forecast'] = FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE\\n                record['condition'] = 'FY2027 revenue is at least $350 billion'\\n            else:\\n                record['answers'] = labels\\n                record['answer'] = _answer(\"),\n    15\t    'one_line from the latest why_changed': (R, \"evidence.append({'id': piece['evidence_id'], **{name: piece[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources})\",\n    16\t                                             \"evidence.append({'id': piece['evidence_id'], **{name: piece[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources, 'one_line': (views_db.execute('select why_changed from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone() or {'why_changed': piece['one_line']})['why_changed']})\"),\n    17\t    'event test removed': (R, \"    if key_measure(conn, view_id, as_of) in identity.EVENT_MEASURES:\\n        return 'event'\\n\", ''),\n    18\t    'Yes/No test removed': (R, \"    if len(labels) == 2 and {vocabulary.canonical('label', label) for label in labels} == {'Yes', 'No'}:\\n        return 'yes_no'\\n\", ''),\n    19\t    'check_package without the file-set check': (R, \"        if sorted(names) != sorted(PACKAGE_FILES):\\n            raise\", \"        if False:\\n            raise\"),\n    20\t    'manifest keys unchecked': (R, \"    _keys(manifest, 'manifest', 'the manifest')\\n\", ''),\n    21\t    'check_export without the closed-key check': (R, \"    if set(value) != ALLOWED[kind]:\", \"    if not set(value) >= ALLOWED[kind]:\"),\n    22\t    'check_origins skipping evidence fields': (R, \"            expected_evidence = _expected_evidence(views_db, items_db, view_id, as_of)\\n\",\n    23\t                                               \"            expected_evidence = question['evidence']\\n\"),\n    24\t    'check_origins taking the class from the package': (R, \"            kind = question_class(views_db, view_id, labels, as_of)\\n            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': _open_at(\",\n    25\t                                                        \"            kind = question['class']\\n            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': _open_at(\"),\n    26\t    'check_origins accepting duplicates': (R, \"        packaged = data['questions']\\n\", \"        packaged = list({q['id']: q for q in data['questions']}.values())\\n\"),\n    27\t    'check_origins accepting another order': (R, \"        packaged = data['questions']\\n\",\n    28\t                                              \"        packaged = sorted(data['questions'], key=lambda q: [r['view_id'] for r in views].index(q['id']) if q['id'] in [r['view_id'] for r in views] else -1)\\n\"),\n    29\t    'pipe opened blocking': (R, \"os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK, dir_fd=folder)\", \"os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW, dir_fd=folder)\"),\n    30\t    'store path returned unresolved': (R, \"        raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: a store path may not contain {found}, which the SQLite opener reads as URI syntax')\\n    return real\",\n    31\t                                       \"        raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: a store path may not contain {found}, which the SQLite opener reads as URI syntax')\\n    return path\"),\n    32\t    'check_origins with an inner join': (R, \"            if item is None:\\n                raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {row[\\\"evidence_id\\\"]}\", \"            if item is None:\\n                continue\\n                raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {row[\\\"evidence_id\\\"]}\"),\n    33\t    'check without validating the day': (R, \"        bound = expected_as_of if expected_as_of is not None else resolve(views_db, data['as_of'])\",\n    34\t                                         \"        bound = expected_as_of if expected_as_of is not None else data['as_of']\"),\n    35\t    'builder skipping the staged check': (B, \"counts, data, size = release.check_package(staged, views_db, items_db, expected_as_of=bound)\", \"counts, size = release.check_export(data), 0\"),\n    36\t    'symbolic-link check removed': (R, \"os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK, dir_fd=folder)\", \"os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK, dir_fd=folder)\"),\n    37\t    'duplicate-key check removed': (R, \"    if len(names) != len(set(names)):\", \"    if False:\"),\n    38\t    'switch reason emitted': (R, \"            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': service.is_open_as_of(views_db, view_id, bound), 'class': kind}\",\n    39\t                              \"            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': service.is_open_as_of(views_db, view_id, bound), 'class': kind, 'reason': (views_db.execute('select reason from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)).fetchone() or {'reason': ''})['reason']}\"),\n    40\t    'missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback': (R, \"        if row is None:\\n            raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {evidence_id}: source item {input_id} is not in the items database')\",\n    41\t                                                         \"        if row is None:\\n            row = {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'source_uri': ''}\"),\n    42\t    'publish replaced by os.rename': (R, \"    rename = _no_replace_rename()\\n    if rename is None:\", \"    rename = lambda source, target: os.rename(source, target) or 0\\n    if rename is None:\"),\n    43\t    'the finally removed': (B, \"        if staged is not None:\\n            shutil.rmtree(staged)\\n\", ''),\n    44\t    'staging path not dropped after publish': (B, \"        staged = None                       # published\", \"        pass                                # published\"),\n    45\t    'canonical-day check removed': (R, \"    if day.isoformat() != text:\\n        raise ReleaseRefused\", \"    if False:\\n        raise ReleaseRefused\"),\n    46\t    'key read without its day': (R, \"    return row['measure'] if row is not None and service.visible(conn, row['seq'], as_of) else None\",\n    47\t                                 \"    return row['measure'] if row is not None else None\"),\n    48\t    'null accepted as text': (R, \"        if not isinstance(value[name], str):\", \"        if not (isinstance(value[name], str) or value[name] is None):\"),\n    49\t    'store-path refusal removed': (R, \"    if found:\\n        raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: a store path\", \"    if False:\\n        raise ReleaseRefused(f'{path}: a store path\"),\n    50\t    'writer self-check removed': (R, \"    check_export(data)\\n    return data\\n\", \"    return data\\n\"),\n    51\t    \"a number label written into another question's evidence\": (R, \"evidence.append({'id': piece['evidence_id'], **{name: piece[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources})\",\n    52\t        \"evidence.append({'id': piece['evidence_id'], **{name: piece[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources, **({'one_line': 'Bullish'} if view_id == 'v6' else {})})\"),\n    53\t    'report missing a field': (B, \"    summary = {'ledger': str(args.ledger), 'items': str(args.items), 'as_of': data['as_of'],\", \"    summary = {'ledger': str(args.ledger), 'as_of': data['as_of'],\"),\n    54\t    'report not printed': (B, \"    print(json.dumps(report, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\\n\", \"\"),\n    55\t    'page embed not escaping <': (R, \"EMBED_ESCAPED = ('<', '>', '&', chr(0x2028), chr(0x2029))\", \"EMBED_ESCAPED = ('>', '&', chr(0x2028), chr(0x2029))\"),\n    56\t    'quote written with innerHTML': (R, \"item.appendChild(el('blockquote','evidence-quote',e.quote));\", \"var bq=el('blockquote','evidence-quote');bq.innerHTML=e.quote;item.appendChild(bq);\"),\n    57\t    'source address as a link': (R, \"row.appendChild(el('span','source-address',s.uri));\", \"var ln=document.createElement('a');ln.className='source-address';ln.href=s.uri;ln.textContent=s.uri;row.appendChild(ln);\"),\n    58\t    'package page not compared with its data': (R, \"    if page != render_page(raw):\\n        raise\", \"    if False:\\n        raise\"),\n    59\t    'page hash unchecked': (R, \"    if manifest['page_sha256'] != hashlib.sha256(page).hexdigest():\\n        raise\", \"    if False:\\n        raise\"),\n    60\t    'CSP hash over another script': (R, \"    csp = PAGE_CSP.format(script=_source_hash(PAGE_SCRIPT), style=_source_hash(PAGE_STYLE))\",\n    61\t                                     \"    csp = PAGE_CSP.format(script=_source_hash(PAGE_SCRIPT + ' '), style=_source_hash(PAGE_STYLE))\"),\n    62\t    'publish_report replaced by os.replace': (R, \"        os.link(temporary, path)\\n\", \"        os.replace(temporary, path)\\n        open(temporary, 'w').close()\\n\"),\n    63\t}\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\tdef tree(where):\n    67\t    root = Path(where)\n    68\t    shutil.copytree(REPO / 'src', root / 'src', ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('__pycache__'))\n    69\t    shutil.copytree(REPO / 'scripts', root / 'scripts', ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('__pycache__'))\n    70\t    (root / 'tests').mkdir()\n    71\t    for name in ('test_release.py', 'conftest.py'):\n    72\t        shutil.copy(REPO / 'tests' / name, root / 'tests' / name)\n    73\t    return root\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\tdef run(root):\n    77\t    return subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-m', 'pytest', 'tests/test_release.py', '-q', '-p', 'no:cacheprovider', f'--junitxml={root}/junit.xml'], cwd=root, capture_output=True, text=True,\n    78\t                          env={'PATH': '/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin', 'PYTHONPATH': f'{root}/src:{root}/poc', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE': '1', 'HOME': str(Path.home())}, timeout=900)\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\twith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as base:\n    82\t    control = run(tree(Path(base) / 'control'))\n    83\t    print('control:', 'PASS' if control.returncode == 0 else 'FAIL', control.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1])\n    84\t    if control.returncode != 0:\n    85\t        raise SystemExit('the unmutated control fails: no mutant is judged')\n    86\t    caught = 0\n    87\t    for n, (name, (relative, old, new)) in enumerate(MUTANTS.items()):\n    88\t        root = tree(Path(base) / f'm{n}')\n    89\t        path = root / relative\n    90\t        text = path.read_text()\n    91\t        assert text.count(old) == 1, (name, text.count(old))\n    92\t        path.write_text(text.replace(old, new))\n    93\t        result = run(root)\n    94\t        cases = ElementTree.parse(root / 'junit.xml').getroot().iter('testcase')\n    95\t        outcomes = [(case.get('name'), case.find('failure'), case.find('error')) for case in cases]\n    96\t        failed = [name for name, failure, _ in outcomes if failure is not None   # a test that failed on its own scratch edit is not a catch\n    97\t                  and 'scratch anchor' not in (failure.get('message') or '') + (failure.text or '')]\n    98\t        errors = [name for name, _, error in outcomes if error is not None]\n    99\t        verdict = 'CAUGHT' if failed and not errors else 'MISSED' if not errors else 'ERROR'   # a setup or collection error is not a catch\n   100\t        caught += verdict == 'CAUGHT'\n   101\t        print(f'{verdict}  {name}: {len(failed)} failing: {\", \".join(failed[:6])}' + (f' | errors: {errors[:2]}' if errors else ''))\n   102\t    print(f'{caught} of {len(MUTANTS)} mutants caught')\n32:J1580_PREFIX = 'About $390 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half'   # the system's own forecast used as the forged value\n129:    \"\"\"A forged copy made consistent everywhere but the store: its page made from the forged data again and both hashes refreshed, so\n134:        (package / release.PAGE_FILE).write_bytes(release.render_page(payload))\n137:    manifest['page_sha256'] = hashlib.sha256((package / release.PAGE_FILE).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n194:    forged = out / 'old-1' / 'forged-summary'\n195:    shutil.copytree(package, forged)\n198:    refresh(forged, changed)\n199:    prose = out / 'old-1' / 'forged-manifest'\n204:                           'substituted_into_e2295_refused': refused(ledger, items, forged),\n207:    results['decisive']['forged_value_is_j1580'] = implied.startswith(J1580_PREFIX)\n265:        failures += [] if (packages[name]['format'], packages[name]['allow_list'], delivered['format'], delivered['allow_list']) == (FORMAT, ALLOW_LIST, FORMAT, ALLOW_LIST) else [f'{name}: format or allow-list']\n268:    failures += [] if results['decisive']['forged_value_is_j1580'] else ['the forged value is not the system forecast j1580']\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\"自己的量，别的期间\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n**The one next task: slice 2 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release, the reader's screen (D758 order; D756's screen check).** The release\npage reads only the slice-1 package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite trials, and no idea\nsubmission. A browser check shows the `old-1/v8` screen with its question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", and nothing else. It\nstarts with a design reviewed by the council before code, like slice 1. Commit, publish and deploy remain Alex's.\n\n**Slice 1 is built and accepted at $0 (D759).**\n- Code: `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n- Design: `research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md` revision 11. Result: `RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`.\n- **Reviews:** design councils 74–74j; build councils 75–75g, which accepted it.\n- **Proof:**\n  - 36 release tests; full suite 425;\n  - 31 of 32 mutants caught; the 32nd is equivalent on Python 3.10;\n  - the $0 check on four stores passes every item it names (`poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/`).\n- **What each package holds:**\n  - a number question: its question, its evidence in force and \"Forecast unavailable\";\n  - an event or Yes/No question: its question, evidence and answer labels, with no explanation text.\n- **What makes it safe:**\n  - every package field is checked against its store before one atomic publication that never replaces an existing path;\n  - the system's own forecast placed into a summary is refused.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
