{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"**Slice 2 accepted. All three round-77 findings are closed.** The saved NVIDIA revenue page shows “Forecast unavailable.” Opening it reveals 1,284 evidence groups in the frozen order. Closing and reopening it produces the same screen. The five normal browser visits each recorded one request for the page itself and zero errors. [screen-results.json:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:5) · [Expanded screenshot](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1-v8.png)\n\n### 1. Round 77 and revision 7\n\n| Round-77 finding | What closes it |\n|---|---|\n| Requests and errors were enforced on only one visit | The same check now requires exactly the visited file URL and rejects log errors, exceptions and console errors. It runs after the interactions on desktop, phone, both dated pages and the escaping fixture. All five saved records meet that condition. [release_screen.mjs:135](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:135) · [Recorded results for all five visits:120215](/Users/lchingen/.claude/projects/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109.jsonl:120215) |\n| The light-background negative inherited the machine’s colour scheme | It now explicitly selects light. Chrome recorded a transparent card over the light body, `rgb(245, 242, 235)`. The checker starts at the marker’s own background and found all 19 markers unreadable. [release_screen.mjs:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:88) · [release_screen.mjs:288](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:288) · [screen-results.json:155](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:155) |\n| Several checks could pass for the wrong reason | The whole-page check reads the initial screen before toggling. The hostile quote must match exactly and be visible. I compared the saved inside-card result with the frozen card and found exactly one added forecast line. On the transparent page, all 47 cards existed, zero were visible, the fallback was gone and Chrome recorded zero errors. [release_screen.mjs:152](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:152) · [release_screen.mjs:225](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:225) · [release_screen.mjs:256](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:256) · [screen-results.json:123](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:123) |\n\nThe **one product departure** is the documented comma correction under the same format number. Revision 7 calls for a new format when the template changes. The earlier and final manifests have identical data hashes and different page hashes. I checked that the current checker refuses the earlier page and accepts the final one. This was a pre-release versioning departure with no observed reader-safety impact. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:144) · [Earlier manifest:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23/old-1/manifest.json:1) · [Final manifest:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1/manifest.json:1)\n\n### 2. What the shipped page can show or request\n\nI found **no path in the pinned page to read an outside forecast, execute source text or initiate another request**. The script reads the embedded JSON. It puts quotations and source addresses into text nodes, uses fixed element types and builds evidence only when its question opens. The embed escapes the characters that could terminate its data block. The page policy allows its hashed script and style and forbids connections. [release.py:516](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:516) · [release.py:534](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:534) · [release.py:548](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:548) · [release.py:572](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:572)\n\nAll four saved screen packages passed the current checker. I also observed it read the data, manifest and page once each through the same folder handle. It compares the page with a fresh rendering of those exact data bytes, then verifies the page hash. The complete template matched the hash pinned in test 29. The two dated screens each showed “Answer: Yes” and their own single evidence group. [release.py:464](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:464) · [test_release.py:832](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:832) · [screen-results.json:62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:62) · [screen-results.json:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:85)\n\n### 3. What the browser check proves\n\n**The expectation is independent.** I regenerated all three expected screens in memory from their accepted format-1 packages. Each matched the frozen file, including the dated evidence. The file’s SHA-256 also matched the corrected run. [release_screen_prepare.py:54](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen_prepare.py:54) · [release_screen_prepare.py:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen_prepare.py:86) · [screen-results.json:2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:2)\n\n**All eight negatives showed their intended effect.** In addition to the cases above, the sibling forecast appeared outside the card, the one-line quotes produced 1,220 clipping findings, the clipping wrappers produced 1,284, and the dark-mode copy produced 19 unreadable markers. The fetch copy rendered and produced a security error naming its destination and `connect-src`. [release_screen.mjs:251](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:251) · [release_screen.mjs:274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:274) · [screen-results.json:118](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:118)\n\n**The Chrome observation is faithful when attributed to the right run.** The port-8788 probe recorded one document request, a security error naming `default-src`, a JavaScript refusal and a rendered page. It recorded no fetch request. The final port-59999 check establishes rendering and the named `connect-src` refusal. Its saved booleans do not establish an exact error count for that visit. [Raw probe output:119530](/Users/lchingen/.claude/projects/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109.jsonl:119530) · [screen-results.json:118](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:118)\n\n### 4. Accuracy of the result page\n\nThe headline measurements hold: **0.049 seconds**, **5,794,595 page bytes**, and a five-line Morningstar quote between pixels 36 and 374 on the 390-pixel screen. The saved test output confirms 429 passing tests, 40 passing release tests, all six slice-2 code mutants caught and 37 of 38 caught overall. The four-store check passed. [screen-results.json:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:5) · [screen-results.json:48](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:48) · [Mutant results:120084](/Users/lchingen/.claude/projects/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109.jsonl:120084) · [Final test output:120140](/Users/lchingen/.claude/projects/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109.jsonl:120140)\n\nTwo wording corrections would make the report exact. Neither affects acceptance.\n\n- **Order of the forgery checks.** Both recorded refusal reasons are correct. The forged summary reaches the store comparison. The forged manifest’s extra `note` is rejected **before** the page comparison, so the report’s phrase “checks after the page” applies only to the summary. [RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md:30) · [release.py:470](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:470) · [results.json:44598](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23i/results.json:44598)\n- **Scope of the visibility claims.** The initial collapsed reading applies to the four whole-page visits. The light-and-dark comparison applies to `old-1`. The dated pages were each read in one scheme. The escaping fixture was opened directly and checked for exact visible text, zero images and clean browser signals. That satisfies its specified test. [RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md:48](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md:48) · [release_screen.mjs:213](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:213) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:279](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:279)\n\nThe review was read-only. No further browser run is needed for this verdict."}}
